<section class="section reveal" id="section3">
<span class="section-label">Advanced Techniques</span>
<h2>Optimization and Advanced Strategies</h2>
<p>Beyond basic patterns, world-class systems employ advanced techniques for extreme performance, reliability, and cost efficiency. These techniques require deep understanding of your specific workloads and constraints.</p>

<h3>Technique 1: Request Coalescing</h3>
<p>When multiple users request the same computation, execute it once and return results to all. This dramatically reduces redundant work and cost at scale.</p>

<h3>Technique 2: Adaptive Timeouts</h3>
<p>Rather than fixed timeouts, set timeouts based on system load and request deadline. High load means more aggressive timeouts; low load means wait longer for better results.</p>

<h3>Technique 3: Resource Prediction</h3>
<p>Use past performance data to predict which requests will be slow or expensive. Prioritize fast requests or reject expensive ones proactively rather than waiting for failure.</p>

<div class="key-takeaway">
<h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
<ul>
<li>Request coalescing reduces redundant computation at scale</li>
<li>Adaptive timeouts balance latency and system health dynamically</li>
<li>Predictive mechanisms enable proactive rather than reactive optimization</li>
<li>Measure before optimizing: understand where time and money actually go</li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>

