<section class="section reveal" id="section4">
<span class="section-label">Integration and Operations</span>
<h2>Integrating into Your Production System</h2>
<p>These patterns don't exist in isolation. They integrate with your data pipelines, monitoring infrastructure, deployment systems, and operational procedures. Success requires treating them as part of a cohesive whole.</p>

<h3>Integration Checklist</h3>
<ul>
<li>Monitoring: Can you measure the performance of each component?</li>
<li>Alerting: Will you know when something breaks?</li>
<li>Runbooks: Do you have procedures for common failure scenarios?</li>
<li>Testing: Have you tested failure scenarios in production-like environments?</li>
<li>Documentation: Can new team members understand the architecture?</li>
</ul>

<div class="why-matters">
<h4>🌍 Why This Matters</h4>
<p><strong>In Fast-Moving Organizations:</strong> Good architecture enables teams to deploy confidently multiple times daily. Bad architecture forces painful big-bang releases.</p>
<p><strong>In Reliability-Critical Systems:</strong> Architecture fundamentally determines what failure modes are possible. Design determines whether failures cascade or gracefully degrade.</p>
</div>

<div class="key-takeaway">
<h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
<ul>
<li>Architecture is not academic—measure its real-world impact on cost, speed, and reliability</li>
<li>Document architectural constraints and assumptions for future teams</li>
<li>Test architectural changes before deploying to production</li>
<li>Monitor architectural health metrics: latency, error rates, cascade failures</li>
<li>Iterate on architecture as your system grows and requirements change</li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>

