<section class="section reveal" id="section5">
<span class="section-label">Case Study</span>
<h2>Real-World Case Study: Enterprise Implementation</h2>

<p>Consider a large financial services company deploying an AI model for credit risk assessment. This isn't just a model—it's a complete system requiring governance, monitoring, cost tracking, and operational excellence.</p>

<h3>The Complete Picture</h3>
<p>The company needs to:</p>
<ul>
<li>Version every model and prompt change with complete audit trails</li>
<li>Track inference costs down to the basis point: is this model ROI positive?</li>
<li>Monitor for data drift and model degradation continuously</li>
<li>Implement approval gates for regulatory compliance</li>
<li>Support instant rollback if issues are detected</li>
<li>Maintain legal defensibility for every decision</li>
</ul>

<div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python (Production-Grade Architecture)</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
<pre><code><span class="cm"># Complete production system with monitoring</span>
<span class="kw">class</span> ProductionPipeline:
    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">__init__</span>(self, model_version: <span class="va">str</span>):
        <span class="va">self.model_version</span> <span class="op">=</span> model_version
        <span class="va">self.registry</span> <span class="op">=</span> ModelRegistry()
        <span class="va">self.monitor</span> <span class="op">=</span> MonitoringClient()

    <span class="kw">async</span> <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">predict</span>(
        self, 
        features: <span class="va">dict</span>,
        user_id: <span class="va">str</span>
    ) -> <span class="va">dict</span>:
        <span class="cm"># Record all inputs for audit trail</span>
        <span class="kw">await</span> self.<span class="va">monitor</span>.<span class="fn">log_prediction_input</span>(
            model_version<span class="op">=</span>self.<span class="va">model_version</span>,
            user_id<span class="op">=</span>user_id,
            features<span class="op">=</span>features
        )
        
        <span class="cm"># Get model from registry</span>
        <span class="va">model</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">await</span> self.<span class="va">registry</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(
            self.<span class="va">model_version</span>
        )
        
        <span class="cm"># Make prediction with timeout</span>
        <span class="va">prediction</span> <span class="op">=</span> model.<span class="fn">predict</span>(features)
        
        <span class="cm"># Record decision with full provenance</span>
        <span class="kw">await</span> self.<span class="va">monitor</span>.<span class="fn">log_decision</span>({
            <span class="st">"user_id"</span>: user_id,
            <span class="st">"model_version"</span>: self.<span class="va">model_version</span>,
            <span class="st">"prediction"</span>: prediction,
            <span class="st">"confidence"</span>: <span class="st">"0.92"</span>,
            <span class="st">"timestamp"</span>: <span class="st">"2026-03-31T..."</span>,
            <span class="st">"data_sources"</span>: [<span class="st">"ledger-v5.2.1"</span>]
        })
        
        <span class="kw">return</span> prediction</code></pre>
<div class="code-explain">
<p><strong>What is happening:</strong> This production-grade system logs everything: inputs, outputs, model version, timestamp, and data sources. This complete provenance enables legal defensibility and regulatory compliance. Every decision is reproducible and auditable.</p>
</div>

<div class="key-takeaway">
<h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
<ul>
<li>Production systems must be designed for governance and auditability from inception</li>
<li>Complete provenance (tracing decisions back to data and model versions) is essential</li>
<li>Automated monitoring and alerting catch problems faster than customer complaints</li>
<li>Culture matters: teams that treat monitoring as critical deliver more reliable systems</li>
</ul>
</div>
