<section class="section reveal" id="section6">
<span class="section-label">Advanced Topics</span>
<h2>Advanced Operational Techniques</h2>

<p>Beyond the fundamentals, production systems employ advanced techniques to achieve extreme scale, reliability, and cost efficiency. These techniques require deep expertise but deliver outsized returns.</p>

<h3>Technique: Feature Flags and Experimentation</h3>
<p>Deploy code to production but disable features via feature flags. This enables experimentation, gradual rollout, and instant rollback without code changes. Feature flags decouple deployment from activation.</p>

<h3>Technique: Request Prioritization</h3>
<p>Under load, serve high-priority requests (paying customers, critical systems) before low-priority ones (analytics, non-critical features). Use request metadata to determine priority automatically.</p>

<h3>Technique: Distributed Tracing</h3>
<p>Follow requests through your entire system: which components did it touch? Where did time go? Where did failures occur? Distributed traces are essential for debugging production systems.</p>

<div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python (Distributed Tracing)</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
<pre><code><span class="kw">import</span> logging
<span class="kw">from</span> opentelemetry <span class="kw">import</span> trace

<span class="va">tracer</span> <span class="op">=</span> trace.<span class="fn">get_tracer</span>(<span class="st">__name__</span>)

<span class="kw">async</span> <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">process_request</span>(request_id: <span class="va">str</span>):
    <span class="kw">with</span> tracer.<span class="fn">start_as_current_span</span>(
        <span class="st">"process_request"</span>
    ) <span class="kw">as</span> span:
        span.<span class="fn">set_attribute</span>(<span class="st">"request.id"</span>, request_id)
        
        <span class="kw">with</span> tracer.<span class="fn">start_as_current_span</span>(<span class="st">"load_data"</span>):
            data <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">await</span> load_data(request_id)
        
        <span class="kw">with</span> tracer.<span class="fn">start_as_current_span</span>(<span class="st">"model_inference"</span>):
            result <span class="op">=</span> model.<span class="fn">predict</span>(data)
        
        <span class="kw">return</span> result</code></pre>
<div class="code-explain">
<p><strong>What is happening:</strong> Each operation is traced with timing information. If request processing takes 1 second and you see that 800ms went to model inference, you know where to optimize.</p>
</div>

<div class="key-takeaway">
<h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
<ul>
<li>Feature flags enable deployment and experimentation decoupling</li>
<li>Request prioritization ensures critical work completes even under load</li>
<li>Distributed tracing reveals exactly where time and failures occur</li>
<li>These techniques compound: together they enable extreme reliability at scale</li>
<li>Implement them gradually: start with the highest ROI techniques</li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>


